# Tribunal "The Barbarian and the Book": Thrud in Godsreach greets the player
# about his friend Dilborn (10) and, asked to help ("Dilborn", choice 1), follows
# (20). Drathas Nerus holds Dilborn in the Residential Sewers for a gambling debt
# (30). Refusing to pay ("Let him go now or feel my wrath.", choice 3) starts the
# fight; once Drathas, Melur Savil and Alam Merys are dead with Thrud and
# Dilborn alive, dilbornScript logs 160.
# Kills stand in for the fight, before the menu closes: Melur and Alam go for
# Dilborn at once, and his death logs 150 instead (measured). Ref FormIDs carry
# Tribunal.esm's slot 06.
# Run: python -m tools.live.test_instance mwtest --cases <this folder> --fast --checkpoints --stop-on-fail --load mwtest_ms_black_dart --timeout 2400
# See docs/commentary/headless_testing.md#quest-runs

case ms_barbarian_book
run
player->PositionCell 133 74 106 0 "Mournhold, Godsreach"
until 600 "thrud"->GetDistance player < 400
talk thrud
expect GetJournalIndex MS_BarbarianBook == 10
ask Dilborn
choose 1
expect GetJournalIndex MS_BarbarianBook == 20
bye
run
player->PositionCell -212 6000 746 0 "Old Mournhold: Residential Sewers"
until 300 GetPCCell "Old Mournhold: Residential Sewers" == 1
until 600 "drathas nerus"->GetDistance player < 400
talk drathas nerus
expect GetJournalIndex MS_BarbarianBook == 30
ask owe me money
choose 3
console 067D404C.kill
console 06AB1305.kill
console 066FFF12.kill
bye
defend
until 900 GetJournalIndex MS_BarbarianBook == 160
end
